text:
Not bug. React `StrictMode` behavior (React 18+). Dev only: React mount component, run effects, run cleanup, run effects again. Purpose: catch effects missing cleanup. Prod build skip this.

Check `main.jsx` / `index.js`:

```jsx
<React.StrictMode>
  <App />
</React.StrictMode>
```

Right fix: make effect safe to run twice. Write cleanup, don't remove StrictMode.

Subscription/listener:

```jsx
useEffect(() => {
  const onResize = () => setW(window.innerWidth);
  window.addEventListener('resize', onResize);
  return () => window.removeEventListener('resize', onResize);
}, []);
```

Fetch:

```jsx
useEffect(() => {
  const ctrl = new AbortController();
  fetch(url, { signal: ctrl.signal })
    .then(r => r.json())
    .then(setData)
    .catch(e => { if (e.name !== 'AbortError') throw e; });
  return () => ctrl.abort();
}, [url]);
```

Or ignore flag:

```jsx
useEffect(() => {
  let ignore = false;
  fetchData().then(d => { if (!ignore) setData(d); });
  return () => { ignore = true; };
}, []);
```

Two network requests in dev still show in Network tab. Normal. Only one result gets used.

True one-time app init (analytics, SDK setup): move outside component, or guard with module-level flag:

```jsx
let didInit = false;
function App() {
  useEffect(() => {
    if (didInit) return;
    didInit = true;
    initSdk();
  }, []);
}
```

Avoid `useRef` guard hack for data fetch. It hide missing cleanup, and React may break it later (Offscreen/Activity reuse).

Removing `<StrictMode>` stop double run, but you lose dev checks. Not recommended.
